  "final_response": "The test passes now.\n\n**Change:** In `parse_date` (app/parser.py), the three components from `split_date` were being unpacked as `year, day, month`, which swapped the month and day for the ISO-style `YYYY-MM-DD` / `YYYY/MM/DD` inputs the function documents. Since the returned tuple was then built as `(year, month, day)`, the swap showed up in the output — e.g. `\"2026-03-07\"` returned `(2026, 7, 3)`.\n\nI changed the unpacking to `year, month, day`, matching the order the parts actually appear in the input string. One line changed; the `split_date` helper and its `ImportError` fallback were left alone.",
